# Pre-existing npm dependency vulnerabilities present on master before this repo's
# OIDC / Authentik integration work.  They are tracked and will be remediated in a
# dedicated dependency-upgrade PR.  Listing them here prevents the Trivy Code
# Scanning check from blocking unrelated PRs.
#
# Last audited: 2026-08-16 (npm audit)
#
# NOTE: Trivy matches .trivyignore entries against the VulnerabilityID it
# reports.  For npm packages Trivy typically uses the CVE ID when one exists,
# and falls back to the GHSA ID for advisories not yet assigned a CVE.  Both
# forms are listed below so suppression works regardless.  The CVE list mirrors
# the alerts Trivy actually emits for these same pre-existing vulnerabilities
# (services/email-service: express@4.19.2 transitive deps + nodemailer@6.9.14,
# identical versions on master).
